      "issue_id": "SCI_LABEL_OVERLAP",
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Sister A/B (later Daughter A/B) labels are both placed 'up' at centers only 0.44 apart, so they render as overlapping, unreadable text ('SistSister B', 'DauDaughter') from 0-9s. Chromatid identity is distinguishable only by color; the declared identities cannot be read, weakening verification of which sister attaches to which pole.",
      "root_cause_stage": "SCENE_IR",
      "target_objects": [
        "sister_A",
        "sister_B"
      ],
      "target_events": [
        "metaphase",
        "anaphase"
      ],
      "repair_scope": "assembly_geometry",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        "Label bounding boxes of sister_A and sister_B do not intersect at any sampled time in metaphase or anaphase",
        "Each full label string ('Sister A','Sister B','Daughter A','Daughter B') is legible in rendered frames",
        "Label anchors continue to track their chromatid centers during separation motion"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Mechanism verified: left pole attaches kinetochore_A/sister_A, right pole kinetochore_B/sister_B (measured endpoint distance 0.0); bipolar relations exist before split; sister_cohesion removed at ~6s while positions remain coincident, then monotonic poleward motion to +/-2.8 with kinetochores and microtubule ends tracking (0.0 gap). Two persistent chromatid instances, no cloning; role change to daughter_chromosome is metadata, consistent with F1/F5/F8.",
    "Schematic single duplicated chromosome and outward-facing kinetochores are declared allowed simplifications, not errors.",
    "Uncertainty: the final supplied image is an unrelated 'Grid Visual'/SVM slide with no registered IDs. Treated as the spatial reference grid per instructions; if it is actually appended to the delivered MP4, it is out-of-scope content requiring removal and human confirmation.",
    "Early microtubule tips at +/-0.285 vs kinetochore +/-0.22 leave a ~0.065 transient gap before connect; within schematic tolerance and resolved on attachment, not flagged."
  ],
